==English==

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# The act or process by which one thing is embedded in another.
# {{lb|en|mathematics}} A map which maps a subspace (smaller structure) to the whole space (larger structure).
# {{lb|en|machine learning|AI}} A representation of a unit of [[text#Noun|text]] (such as a [[word#Noun|word]] or [[token#Noun|token]]) as a [[vector#Noun|vector]], which [[encode#Verb|encodes]] the [[context#Noun|context]] in which it is used.
#* {{RQ:NYT|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20230517091124/https://www.nytimes.com/2023/05/01/science/ai-speech-language.html|author=Oliver Whang|title=A.I. Is Getting Better at Mind-Reading|date=1 May 2023|passage=A few years ago, Dr. [Alexander] Huth noticed that particular pieces of these maps — so-called context '''embeddings''', which capture the semantic features, or meanings, of phrases — could be used to predict how the brain lights up in response to language.}}

